description:
## Interfaces
So far your objects have no type checking. You could accidentally misspell a property or forget one. Interfaces fix that.

An interface defines the SHAPE of an object:
```ts
interface Video {
    title: string;
    views: number;
    isPublic: boolean;
}

const video: Video = {
    title: "Cat Falls",
    views: 5000,
    isPublic: true
};
```

Now TypeScript enforces:
- All properties must exist
- All properties must be the correct type
- No extra properties allowed

### Optional properties:
```ts
interface Video {
    title: string;
    views: number;
    description?: string;  // optional
}
```


